workedExamples.question_text:
A rectangle has width:length $=5:7$ and length $26.6$ cm. Find its perimeter.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4.2,3);
\node[below] at (2.1,0) {$26.6$ cm};
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$?$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Length represents $7$ parts.
$1\text{ part}=26.6\div7=3.8\text{ cm}$
Width: $5\times3.8=19\text{ cm}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4.2,3);
\node[below] at (2.1,0) {$26.6$ cm};
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$19$ cm};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}P=2\times(19+26.6)\\&=91.2\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

